        "description": "Seven people have died after a passenger boat capsized near northern Cyprus.\n \nSearch and rescue operations are under way to find 23 people missing, said \u00dcnal \u00dcstel, prime minister of the self-declared Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus.\n \nHe says 267 people were on board the vessel when it capsized, and 237 have been rescued.\n \nThe boat left from the northern Cypriot port of Kyrenia at 11:58 local time (09:58 BST) and officials said it capsized around four nautical miles into its journey to Turkey.\n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\n#BBCNews",
