        "description": "At least 734 people have died and more than 2,400 people are missing in Nepal, local officials say, after flash floods on Wednesday, triggered by a glacier collapse.\n\nIn Tibet, the official death toll is 16, with 546 reported to be missing, according to Chinese state media. \n\nNearly 20,000 security forces are deployed in rescue efforts on the Nepal-Tibet border as the UN says rough terrain and rain is making aid delivery \"extremely difficult\u201d.  \n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\n#Nepal #Tibet #BBCNews",
